# Speech tape — segment CHECKPOINT cadence

Extends `checkpoint-discipline` § Window anchor · § Resume pickup stack layer 2c.
Doctrine: speech tape persists **verbal dialogue** across tabs by pouring from
**checkpoint-bounded cells** (`scope=last_session` keeps tip CP ordinal and
ordinal+1 only). Dialogue on an attended `transcript_id` that never crosses a CP
boundary is **not** reliably inherited by a fresh-tab `resume` — only the tip CP
fold, card, and bounded residue are.

**Two orthogonal CP triggers — do not merge:**

| Trigger | What it folds | When |
|---|---|---|
| **Bus fold** | BINDs, commits, open line, artifact anchors, `#turn` residue | Residue after tip CP would be lost to the bundle, or open line changes (`FIX-18` class) |
| **Speech segment seal** | Attended orchestrator **dialogue** into a new cell for tape pour | This rule — below |

`¬` “one CP per dogfood” for bus-only fence AC **does not** waive segment CP when
the attended tab accumulated judgment dialogue worth handing off.

## Bind — when to post a segment CHECKPOINT

On **`role:root`** houses, attended IDE **orchestrator** tab (pools row: Multitask
OFF, CHECKPOINT/confer/tab-launch — not WORK implement), post a segment CP **before**
the operator or seat opens a **fresh tab** `resume <root>` (or hop clone) **when any**
of:

1. **Handoff intent** — operator will continue the arc on a new tab and expects the
   successor to know *what was said and decided* on this tab, not only bus tip state.
2. **Judgment segment closed** — a bind/land/verify/eval/relay leg finished on this
   tab (e.g. architect BIND harvested, commit landed + dogfood verdict, dispatch
   closeout relayed). One segment CP per **closed judgment leg**, not per tool call.
3. **Material dialogue** — since the last CP on **this** `transcript_id`, the attended
   session gained non-trivial reasoning the operator would treat as lost if the tab
   closed (multi-turn debug, operator pushback adjudicated, fork ranked).
4. **Pre-fresh-tab gate (recommended default)** — immediately before minting a fresh
   work tab for `resume <root>` when this orchestrator tab holds the live arc context.

**Exempt (segment CP not required):**

- Mechanical dogfood where AC is structural only (journal/fence) **and** no judgment
  dialogue needs inheritance — bus fold CP optional.
- Child/work/MONITOR lanes (`spine≠root`) — no root tape pour; use CLOSEOUT/sidecar.
- Mid-implement WORK tab — CLOSEOUT on implement lane, not root segment CP.

## Required shape (segment CP)

Every segment CP on a continuity root **must** include:

1. **`## Anchor`** with attended window (same turn as post):
   `Window: transcript_id=<this-tab-uuid> · turns@cp=<K>`
   `K` from `session_close_preflight` / `assemble_transcript` on that JSONL —
   hand counts forbidden (`checkpoint-discipline` § Window anchor).
2. **`Highlight`** — one sentence: segment verdict (what closed on this tab).
3. **Residue** — bus fold only (commits, binds, next leg); **¬** paste full dialogue
   into CP body — dialogue lives in the tape cell, not the CHECKPOINT prose wall.
4. **Supersede** prior tip CP when the segment changes Settled/Live/Next for the house.

**Tab title:** `. {id} {slug}` on post (`operator-posture`).

## Fresh-tab resume law (successor tab)

After segment CP on orchestrator tab **T₁** with window **W₁**:

- Fresh tab **T₂** `resume <root>` inherits **tip CP fold + card + last_session tape**
  from cells bounded at tip — **not** T₁'s full JSONL unless W₁ was sealed into a cell.
- Successor **¬** claim to be a “clone” of T₁; it is a **reconstituted** seat.
- If orientation cites stale pre-segment residue while tip CP is current ⇒ missing
  segment CP on T₁ or `FIX-18` bundle gap — fix cadence, not “Reload Window”.

## Forbidden

| Forbidden | Why |
|---|---|
| CP per bus INFO/dispatch admit | Bus residue only; no speech cell |
| CP without `Window:` on root speech handoff | Tape cannot bind dialogue to a cell |
| `Window:` pointing at a **different** tab than the one that held the dialogue | Split-brain inheritance (d6900bc0 / d556c84f class) |
| Linear thread read instead of tip CP + envelope | `checkpoint-discipline` § Resume |
| Segment CP on WORK implement tab as root substitute | Wrong pool; root CP on orchestrator |

## Relation to consolidation / FIX-18

- **Consolidation** (10303 harvest) folds graph claims — **not** verbatim attended dialogue.
- **FIX-18** (residue in resume bundle) helps bus orientation — **not** full speech persistence.
- Until async consolidation replaces high-frequency segment seal, **prefer segment CP**
  over hoping one tip CP covers a long orchestrator session.

